# Bitcraftly SEO Standards

Apply these standards whenever implementing or modifying pages that impact search engine visibility.

This rule complements:

- Bitcraftly-Engineering-Standards.mdc
- Bitcraftly-Architecture-Protection-Rules.mdc
- Bitcraftly-Accessibility-Standards.mdc
- Bitcraftly-Performance-Standards.mdc

---

# SEO Goals

Every public page should:

- Be crawlable
- Load quickly
- Be accessible
- Have unique metadata
- Provide meaningful content
- Support structured data where appropriate

---

# Metadata

Every public page should define:

- title
- description
- keywords (when useful)
- canonical URL
- robots directives

Prefer Next.js Metadata API.

Avoid duplicate titles and descriptions.

---

# Open Graph

Include:

- og:title
- og:description
- og:image
- og:url
- og:type

Ensure previews look correct when shared.

---

# Twitter Cards

Provide:

- twitter:card
- twitter:title
- twitter:description
- twitter:image

---

# Structured Data

Use JSON-LD whenever appropriate.

Examples:

- Organization
- LocalBusiness
- Service
- FAQ
- Breadcrumb
- Article
- WebSite

Do not add fake structured data.

---

# Headings

Every page should have:

- One H1
- Logical H2-H6 hierarchy
- Descriptive section headings

Avoid keyword stuffing.

---

# URLs

Prefer:

- short
- readable
- lowercase
- hyphen-separated

Avoid:

- random IDs
- unnecessary query parameters
- duplicate routes

---

# Internal Linking

Prefer:

- descriptive anchor text
- logical navigation
- contextual links

Avoid:

- "Click here"
- "Read more"
- orphan pages

---

# Images

Every image should:

- have meaningful alt text
- use optimized formats
- define dimensions
- lazy load when appropriate

Decorative images:

- alt=""

---

# Content

Content should:

- answer user intent
- remain unique
- be easy to scan
- use meaningful headings
- avoid duplication

Never generate filler content.

---

# Performance & SEO

Protect:

- Core Web Vitals
- Mobile usability
- Accessibility
- Crawlability

Performance improvements should never reduce SEO quality.

---

# Technical SEO

Support:

- sitemap.xml
- robots.txt
- canonical URLs
- metadata
- Open Graph
- structured data

Avoid duplicate canonical URLs.

---

# AI Behaviour

When generating pages:

- Preserve metadata.
- Do not remove structured data.
- Do not create duplicate titles.
- Prefer semantic HTML.
- Keep URLs SEO friendly.
- Explain SEO trade-offs when relevant.

---

# Verification Checklist

Before completing a task verify:

- Metadata exists.
- Title is unique.
- Description is unique.
- Heading hierarchy is correct.
- Images include appropriate alt text.
- Structured data remains valid.
- Accessibility remains compliant.
- Internal links remain functional.

---

# Definition of Done

SEO requirements are satisfied when:

- Metadata is complete.
- Structured data is valid.
- Accessibility is preserved.
- Core Web Vitals are not negatively affected.
- The page remains crawlable and indexable.